# WHAT IT COVERS: the first capture in the corpus from a 120 fps source shown at 60 with no
# frame generation, and the first with -src 120 declared: the comb lock runs at 8333 us, every
# second source frame is passed over by design, and the lag is the 60 Hz present period plus
# the 75 ms. Spider-Man, 53.8 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured through
# Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on 35ce285, the step tolerance at 18%, the long-gap rule
# at 100 ms and the split-pair rule off. It carries src_hint 120 and step_tolerance_pct 18. The
# game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 77 times (86 an hour) and never stalled for 100 ms or more, so
# the long-gap rule never drew a present. The lock released 451 times (503 an hour, where the
# KCD streams release about 6 to 10 an hour), so this capture is mostly the lock letting go
# and re-engaging on a fast source. The worst blend run, 16 presents in the field, starts at
# 1809.85 s, 8 s after a 27 ms hitch.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 28.108 s, from the 3743
# marked frames in its first 62 s, matched within 0.48 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 3240.7 s with no holes; it opens on gameplay and ends on the pause menu, which opens between
# video time 3228.7 s and 3230.7 s, so the cut is 28.1 s to 3256.8 s. Inside the cut, 2 seconds
# in 2 runs fall out of the 120 fps regime, each a single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, with the source rate and the step
# tolerance at the settings the keys name, so the two lines are comparable. The replay line (the
# plain arm, no dejitter) reads synth 2.3% against 2.2%, worst run 14 against 16, runs >= 50 0
# against 0 and pull wraps 180 against 171. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran,
# the worst run is 16 at the same present as the field's, hence max_worst_run_dejit 16 beside
# the plain arm's 14. Counted over the window, replay
# against field: synthesized presents 4278 against 4345, repeats 0 against 0. The replay makes
# 479 moves, none late, against the field's 491; 217 of 480 land more than 2 ms from a real
# frame, a quarter of this source's period. The lock released 440 times on the replay against
# 451 in the field, 368 of them within 0.50 ms and 45 more within 150 ms; on the field's own
# targets 420 match. Dejitter found 11% of batches late on the whole run (KCD runs about
# 0.3%), the same as on the earlier 120 fps stream without -src.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
